possible causes and thirty maintenance

6
00:00:21,144 --> 00:00:25,369
minutes. Each possible cause points to a
different subsystem and a testable

7
00:00:25,444 --> 00:00:30,603
failure mode. The exercise rewards a
testable explanation, not a fast guess.

8
00:00:35,048 --> 00:00:39,773
I begin with P1, repeating the same PIN
motion, and commit a forecast for

9
00:00:39,823 --> 00:00:44,423
each cause before observing anything. Here
every row predicts refusal.

10
00:00:44,473 --> 00:00:47,873
Because that result would not distinguish
the causes, the deterministic

11
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:52,498
Skeptic asks me to reconsider the test. It
uses my submitted forecast and

12
00:00:52,548 --> 00:00:55,698
current public state; it does not need the
hidden fault to raise that

13
00:00:55,748 --> 00:01:00,288
question. I switch to P3 and predict that
key three completes under H1 and

14
00:01:00,338 --> 00:01:06,088
H4, but is refused under H2 and H3. This
splits the four explanations into

15
00:01:06,163 --> 00:01:10,038
two groups. Only after I commit those
predictions do I run the five-minute

16
00:01:10,088 --> 00:01:15,769
test. The observed completion leaves two
